LJ4 replay 1
# movemacro_six_shapes (design 3.6, 17 s7, 10 W3 acceptance 4; owner movement): one homed 16-bit MAC 500 per system
# macro type 1..6 (amplitude 127, cycle byte 32 = 3.2 s = 128 ticks, so the index moves an exact 32 per tick; type 3
# with tilt cycle 64: its tilt index runs at half speed, the figure eight of 17 s7.3; step 512 on the Stepped Ellipse)
# and fixture 7 = System Ellipse with delay 64 (a quarter cycle back). Every expect_pair below is generated by
# 17-position_ref.py (fixture_output(HOME, macro_offset(..))) on the engine's integer tables (tools/gen_vectors.py
# mm_int_tables); the generator lines are in the W3 movement record of docs/w3-contracts.md.
# NOTE ME-22: pan / tilt pairs move as one 16-bit value (LSB non-zero on the intermediate ticks, 65497 = 0xFFD9).
# NOTE 04 s4.5: fixture 8 runs Bezier shape 1 (type 7, the beziershapeeditor.gif diamond, straight segments): a node
# every 1024 points, normalised to +-32767, so idx 0 / 512 / 1024 give tilt 0 / 16383 / 32768 and pan 32768 / 49153 / 65535.
# NOTE ME-35: the sequence sits in cue slots 1 AND 2; the per-fixture index still moves one step per tick (expect_mm).
# NOTE 03 s5.11: macro_ctl 45 % at 130 (127 -> 57), Freeze 140-149 holds the index, Run at 150, Fade out 1000 ms from
# 160 (gain 128 at 180 -> 45 * 128 / 256 = 22 %), amplitude 0 at 200 (home), Macros On at 210 (45 % again).
